  "guide_share_label": "推荐给好友",
  "guide_nutriscore_v2_title": "Nutri-Score 正在演变：为您解释！",
  "@guide_nutriscore_v2_title": {
    "description": "The title of the guide (please don't forget the use of non-breaking spaces)"
  },
  "guide_nutriscore_v2_what_is_nutriscore_title": "什么是 Nutri-Score？",
  "guide_nutriscore_v2_what_is_nutriscore_paragraph1": "Nutri-Score 是一个旨在通知您有关**食品营养质量**的标志。",
  "@guide_nutriscore_v2_what_is_nutriscore_paragraph1": {
    "description": "Text between asterisks (eg: **My Text**) means text in bold. Please try to keep it."
  },
  "guide_nutriscore_v2_what_is_nutriscore_paragraph2": "The color code varies from dark green (**A**) for the **healthiest** products to dark red (**E**) for the **less healthy** ones.",
  "@guide_nutriscore_v2_what_is_nutriscore_paragraph2": {
    "description": "Text between asterisks (eg: **My Text**) means text in bold. Please try to keep it."
  },
  "guide_nutriscore_v2_nutriscore_a_caption": "Nutri-Score A 标志",
  "guide_nutriscore_v2_why_v2_title": "为什么 Nutri-Score 要演变？",
  "guide_nutriscore_v2_why_v2_intro": "Nutri-Score 公式**正在演变**以提供更好的建议：",
  "guide_nutriscore_v2_why_v2_arg1_title": "更好地评估所有饮料",
  "guide_nutriscore_v2_why_v2_arg1_text": "在新算法中，添加糖的**牛奶**、**乳制饮品**和**植物**饮品的对比评分有了更好的区分。",
  "guide_nutriscore_v2_why_v2_arg2_title": "更好的饮料排名",
  "guide_nutriscore_v2_why_v2_arg2_text": "The **sugar content** is better taken into account and favors **lowly sweetened** drinks.\\n**Sweeteners will also be penalized**: diet sodas will be downgraded from a B rating to between C and E. Water remains the recommended drink.",
  "guide_nutriscore_v2_why_v2_arg3_title": "Salt and sugar penalized",
  "guide_nutriscore_v2_why_v2_arg3_text": "**太甜**或**太咸**的产品其**评级将进一步下调**。",
  "guide_nutriscore_v2_why_v2_arg4_title": "油和鱼内的分级",
  "guide_nutriscore_v2_why_v2_arg4_text": "某些**高脂鱼类**和**富含好脂肪的油**的评级将会提高。",
  "guide_nutriscore_v2_why_v2_arg5_title": "限制红肉",
  "guide_nutriscore_v2_why_v2_arg5_text": "**应该限制红肉**的消费。这就是为什么**家禽在比较中将获得更好的排名**。",
  "guide_nutriscore_v2_new_logo_title": "如何区分旧版 Nutri-Score 和新版计算？",
  "guide_nutriscore_v2_new_logo_text": "从现在起，徽标可以显示“**新计算**”字样，以澄清这确实是新的计算方法。",
  "guide_nutriscore_v2_new_logo_image_caption": "新 Nutri-Score 的标志",
  "guide_nutriscore_v2_where_title": "在哪里可以找到新的 Nutri-Score 计算？",
  "guide_nutriscore_v2_where_paragraph1": "Nutri-Score 在7个国家实行：法国、德国、比利时、西班牙、卢森堡、荷兰和瑞士。",
  "guide_nutriscore_v2_where_paragraph2": "制造商在法令签署后最迟有**2年时间****用新计算方法**取代旧计算方法。",
  "guide_nutriscore_v2_where_paragraph3": "无需等待，您**现在就可以在 OpenFoodFacts 应用程序中**找到新的计算方法，即使制造商尚未更新评分。",
  "guide_nutriscore_v2_unchanged_title": "没有改变的是什么",
  "guide_nutriscore_v2_unchanged_paragraph1": "Nutri-Score 是一项旨在**衡量营养质量**的评分。它是有关**超加工食品**的 **NOVA 分类系统的补充**（在应用程序中也有提供）。",
  "guide_nutriscore_v2_unchanged_paragraph2": "对于制造商，Nutri-Score 的显示**仍然是可选的**。",
  "guide_greenscore_title": "Green-Score",
  "@guide_greenscore_title": {
    "description": "The title of the guide (please don't forget the use of non-breaking spaces)"
  },
  "guide_greenscore_what_is_greenscore_title": "什麼是綠色分數？",
  "guide_greenscore_what_is_greenscore_paragraph1": "Green-Score 是一個標誌，旨在告知您**食品對環境的影響**。",
  "@guide_greenscore_what_is_greenscore_paragraph1": {
    "description": "Text between asterisks (eg: **My Text**) means text in bold. Please try to keep it."
  },
  "guide_greenscore_what_is_greenscore_paragraph2": "顏色代碼從代表**影響最小**產品的深綠色（**A+**）到代表**影響最大**產品的深紅色（**F**）不等。",
  "@guide_greenscore_what_is_greenscore_paragraph2": {
    "description": "Text between asterisks (eg: **My Text**) means text in bold. Please try to keep it."
  },
  "guide_greenscore_logos_caption": "Green-Score 標誌",
  "guide_greenscore_lca_title": "核心：生命週期評估（LCA）",
  "guide_greenscore_lca_arg1_title": "食品類別的科學評估",
  "guide_greenscore_lca_arg1_text1": "對於每個產品類別，使用來自 Agribalyse 環境資料庫（由 ADEME 和 INRAE 設計）的資料建立一個**基準**分數。",
  "guide_greenscore_lca_arg1_text2": "**生命週期分析**是一種進行多階段、多標準環境評估的標準化評估方法。",
  "guide_greenscore_lca_arg1_text3": "**其測量：**",
  "guide_greenscore_lca_arg2_title": "6個生產步驟",
  "guide_greenscore_lca_arg2_agriculture": "农业",
  "guide_greenscore_lca_arg2_processing": "加工",
  "guide_greenscore_lca_arg2_packaging": "包装",
  "guide_greenscore_lca_arg2_transportation": "运输",
  "guide_greenscore_lca_arg2_distribution": "分销",
  "guide_greenscore_lca_arg2_consumption": "消费",
  "guide_greenscore_lca_arg3_title": "14項環境影響指標",
  "guide_greenscore_lca_arg3_text1": "氣候變遷/碳足跡",
  "guide_greenscore_lca_arg3_text2": "臭氧層損耗",
  "guide_greenscore_lca_arg3_text3": "電離輻射",
  "guide_greenscore_lca_arg3_text4": "土地",
  "guide_greenscore_lca_arg3_text5": "水和能源的使用",
  "guide_greenscore_lca_arg3_text6": "空氣污染",
  "guide_greenscore_lca_arg3_text7": "海水和淡水（顆粒、酸化、富營養化）",
  "guide_greenscore_lca_arg3_text8": "資源枯竭。",
  "guide_greenscore_bonuses_penalties_title": "獎金和罰款",
  "guide_greenscore_bonuses_penalties_intro": "为了奖励某类产品中较好的产品，我们然后**根据几个标准应用奖金和惩罚**：",
  "guide_greenscore_bonuses_penalties_arg1_title": "生产方式",
  "guide_greenscore_bonuses_penalties_arg1_text": "对于拥有**保证环境效益的官方标签、标记或认证**（有机、公平贸易、HVE、Label Rouge、Bleu Blanc Cœur、MSC/ASC）的产品，将获得**奖金**。",
  "guide_greenscore_bonuses_penalties_arg2_title": "成分來源",
  "guide_greenscore_bonuses_penalties_arg2_text": "根据成分的原产地颁发**奖金**。此奖金考虑到**对运输的影响**以及每个生产国的**环境政策**。",
  "guide_greenscore_bonuses_penalties_arg3_title": "濒危物种",
  "guide_greenscore_bonuses_penalties_arg3_text": "对包含对**生物多样性和生态系统造成重大负面影响**的成分的产品（例如棕榈油，其生产导致大规模的森林砍伐）给予**惩罚**。",
  "guide_greenscore_bonuses_penalties_arg4_title": "包装",
  "guide_greenscore_bonuses_penalties_arg4_text": "计算**惩罚**以考虑**包装的循环性**（使用可回收原材料和可回收性）以及过度包装。",
  "guide_greenscore_transparency_title": "需要提高透明度以更好地衡量和减少环境影响",
  "guide_greenscore_transparency_intro1": "为了准确计算 Green-Score，必须获得**包装上可能没有注明的**（例如原产地和每种成分的确切百分比）或很少能以可用形式提供的信息（例如包含所用特定塑料类型的所有包装组件列表）。",
  "guide_greenscore_transparency_intro2": "**当这些信息尚不可用时使用平均值**，但我们现在呼吁大家帮助我们收集这些信息，这对于 Green-Score 以及许多其他用途将非常有用。",
  "guide_greenscore_transparency_arg1_title": "公民如何提供帮助？",
  "guide_greenscore_transparency_arg1_text": "所有公民都可以帮助我们收集和构建产品上存在或可以从中推断出的信息，例如关于**包装**的信息：“Mission Emballages”：对所有食品包装进行的大规模协作清点（法语）。",
  "guide_greenscore_transparency_arg2_title": "製造商如何提供協助",
  "guide_greenscore_transparency_arg2_text": "製造商可以透過我們為生產商提供的免費平台直接向我們發送他們的資訊。",
  "guide_greenscore_better_product_title": "哪種產品對地球比較好？",
  "guide_greenscore_better_product_arg1_title": "很難說",
  "guide_greenscore_better_product_arg1_text": "選擇永續食品是我們為氣候所能做的最強大的事情之一，因為**我們的全球食品系統造成了超過四分之一的溫室氣體排放**。\n（資料來源：Poore & Nemecek，Science，2018）。",
  "guide_greenscore_better_product_arg2_title": "你有力量！",
  "guide_greenscore_better_product_arg2_text": "好消息是，這為我們提供了一種強而有力的變革方法。\n**我們每個人每年大約吃1000餐**。這意味著我們有1000個機會**為地球選擇更美好的未來**！",
  "guide_greenscore_better_product_arg3_title": "幫助承擔責任並做出決定",
  "guide_greenscore_better_product_arg3_text": "選擇永續食品可能感覺很複雜。標籤令人困惑，資訊也常常缺少。 Green-Score 的創建旨在簡化這一過程，為您提供**清晰**、**基於科學**且**透明**的食品環境評級，就在您需要的時候：購物時。",
  "guide_greenscore_better_product_arg4_title": "透明度",
  "guide_greenscore_better_product_arg4_text": "與專有標籤不同，Green-Score 計算**完全開放**，並且**任何人都可以驗證**。",
  "guide_nova_title": "The overall purpose of ultra-processing is to create branded, convenient (durable, ready to consume), attractive (hyper-palatable) and highly profitable (low-cost ingredients) food products designed to displace all other food groups. Ultra-processed food products are usually packaged attractively and marketed intensively. Ultra-processed food products are usually packaged attractively and marketed intensively. Ultra-processed food products are usually packaged attractively and marketed intensively.",
  "@guide_nova_title": {
    "description": "The title of the guide (please don't forget the use of non-breaking spaces)"
  },
  "guide_nova_what_is_nova_title": "什麼是超加工？",
  "guide_nova_what_is_nova_paragraph1": "NOVA 组通知您有关**食品加工水平**的信息。",
  "@guide_nova_what_is_nova_paragraph1": {
    "description": "Text between asterisks (eg: **My Text**) means text in bold. Please try to keep it."
  },
  "guide_nova_what_is_nova_paragraph2": "NOVA 分類允許根據食品的**工業加工程度**將其分為**4 類**（最低限度加工或未加工食品、烹飪原料、加工食品、超加工食品）。",
  "@guide_nova_what_is_nova_paragraph2": {
    "description": "Text between asterisks (eg: **My Text**) means text in bold. Please try to keep it."
  },
  "guide_nova_logos_caption": "NOVA 標誌",
  "guide_nova_groups_title": "4個NOVA組",
  "guide_nova_groups_intro": "NOVA 有 4 組，有問題的是第 4 組 - 超加工食品。",
  "guide_nova_groups_arg1_title": "低度加工或未加工食品",
  "guide_nova_groups_arg1_text": "未加工（或天然）食品是在与自然分离后，植物（种子、果实、叶子、茎、根）**或动物**（肌肉、内脏、蛋、奶）的**可食用部分**，以及真菌、藻类和水。",
  "guide_nova_groups_arg2_title": "加工的烹飪用食品",
  "guide_nova_groups_arg2_text": "加工过的烹饪配料，如**油、黄油、糖和盐**，是源自第1组食物或来自自然的物质，通过压榨、精炼、研磨、碾磨和干燥等过程制成。",
  "guide_nova_groups_arg3_title": "第三類： 加工食品",
  "guide_nova_groups_arg3_text": "加工食品，如瓶装蔬菜、鱼罐头、糖浆水果、奶酪和新鲜制作的面包，**主要是通过将第2组的盐、油、糖或其他物质添加到第1组**食物中制成。加工包括各种保存或烹饪方法，并且在面包和奶酪的情况下，包括非酒精发酵。大多数加工食品有两到三种成分，可以被识别为第1组食物的修改版本。它们可以单独食用，或者更常见地与其他食物结合食用。",
  "guide_nova_groups_arg4_title": "The overall purpose of ultra-processing is to create branded, convenient (durable, ready to consume), attractive (hyper-palatable) and highly profitable (low-cost ingredients) food products designed to displace all other food groups. Ultra-processed food products are usually packaged attractively and marketed intensively. Ultra-processed food products are usually packaged attractively and marketed intensively. Ultra-processed food products are usually packaged attractively and marketed intensively.",
  "guide_nova_groups_arg4_text": "超加工食品，如软饮料、甜味或咸味包装零食、重组肉制品和预制冷冻食品，**不仅仅是修改过的食物，而是主要或完全由源自食物和添加剂的物质组成的配方**，几乎没有完整的第1组食物。这些配方中的成分通常包括加工食品中也有的成分，如糖、油、脂肪或盐。然而，超加工产品也含有通常不用于烹饪准备的其他能量和营养来源。其中一些直接从食物中提取，如酪蛋白、乳糖、乳清和面筋。",
  "guide_nova_explanations_title": "超加工的問題",
  "guide_nova_explanations_arg1_title": "食品原料的極端加工",
  "guide_nova_explanations_arg1_text": "许多是**来自食品成分的进一步加工**，如氢化或酯交换油、水解蛋白、大豆分离蛋白、麦芽糊精、转化糖和高果糖玉米糖浆。",
  "guide_nova_explanations_arg2_title": "超越純淨食品安全的添加物",
  "guide_nova_explanations_arg2_text": "Additives in ultra-processed foods include some that are also used in processed foods, such as preservatives, antioxidants, and stabilizers. Classes of additives found only in ultra-processed products include those used **to imitate or enhance the sensory qualities of foods or to disguise unpalatable aspects of the final product**. These additives include dyes and other colors, color stabilizers; flavors, flavor enhancers, non-sugar sweeteners; and processing aids such as carbonating, firming, bulking and anti-bulking agents, de-foaming, anti-caking and glazing agents, emulsifiers, sequestrants, and humectants.",
  "guide_nova_explanations_arg3_title": "在家無法完成的處理",
  "guide_nova_explanations_arg3_text": "**使用众多序列工艺**来结合通常许多成分并制造最终产品（因此称为“超加工”）。工艺包括几个**没有家庭对应的工艺**，如氢化和水解、挤压和成型，以及油炸预处理。",
  "guide_nova_explanations_arg4_title": "超加工的掠奪性和財務面",
  "guide_nova_explanations_arg4_text": "**超加工的总体目的是创造品牌化**、**方便**（耐用、即食）、**有吸引力**（高适口性）和**高利润**（低成本成分）的食品产品，旨在取代所有其他食品类别。超加工食品产品通常包装精美并大量营销。",
  "guide_nova_explanations_arg5_title": "对健康的危害",
  "guide_nova_explanations_arg5_text": "自2018年以来，在 NutriNet-Santé 研究中，**超加工食品的摄入与癌症、心血管疾病和糖尿病风险增加之间的首批联系已经被强调**。今天，全球超过90项研究证实了这些发现。\n最强的关联涉及**肥胖、心血管死亡率和抑郁症状**。在儿童中，效果主要表现在体重和脂质失衡。",
  "guide_nova_explanations_arg6_title": "国家建议限制它们",
  "guide_nova_explanations_arg6_text": "一些国家将 NOVA 组用于其饮食指南或目标，例如：\n\n- **🇧🇷 巴西**的饮食指南**建议限制食用**加工食品并避免超加工食品。\n\n- **🇫🇷 法国**2018-2022年公共卫生营养政策目标旨在**将第4组超加工食品的消费量减少20%**。",
  "guide_nova_share_link": "https://world-zh.openfoodfacts.org/nova",
  "@guide_nova_share_link": {
    "comment": "Make sure the link exists before adding a translation"
  },
